    "translation": {
      "en": "My very nature is overcome by the weakness of pity, and my mind is confused about where my duty lies. I am asking You — please tell me clearly what is truly best for me. I am now Your student; I have surrendered to You. Please guide me.",
      "hi": "कृपणता के दोष से मेरा स्वभाव अभिभूत हो गया है और मेरा मन धर्म के विषय में मोहग्रस्त है। मैं आपसे पूछ रहा हूँ, कृपया निश्चित रूप से बताइए कि मेरे लिए क्या श्रेयस्कर है। मैं अब आपका शिष्य हूँ; मैंने आपकी शरण ली है, कृपया मुझे शिक्षा दीजिए।"
    },
    "audioUrl": "audio/2.7_final.m4a"
  },
  {
    "id": "bg-2-13", "name": "BG 2.13", "book": "bg", "sub": "dehino 'smin yathā dehe", "badge": "गी",
    "lines": ["dehino 'smin yathā dehe", "kaumāraṁ yauvanaṁ jarā", "tathā dehāntara-prāptir", "dhīras tatra na muhyati"],
    "words": [
      {"sa": "dehinaḥ", "en": "of the embodied soul", "hi": "देहधारी आत्मा का"},
      {"sa": "asmin", "en": "in this", "hi": "इस"},
      {"sa": "yathā", "en": "as", "hi": "जिस प्रकार"},
      {"sa": "dehe", "en": "in the body", "hi": "शरीर में"},
      {"sa": "kaumāram", "en": "childhood", "hi": "बाल्यावस्था"},
      {"sa": "yauvanam", "en": "youth", "hi": "यौवन"},
      {"sa": "jarā", "en": "old age", "hi": "वृद्धावस्था"},
      {"sa": "tathā", "en": "similarly", "hi": "उसी प्रकार"},
      {"sa": "deha-antara", "en": "a different body", "hi": "दूसरे शरीर की"},
      {"sa": "prāptiḥ", "en": "the attaining of", "hi": "प्राप्ति"},
      {"sa": "dhīraḥ", "en": "the steady/wise person", "hi": "धीर पुरुष"},
      {"sa": "tatra", "en": "at that (change)", "hi": "उस परिवर्तन पर"},
      {"sa": "na muhyati", "en": "is not bewildered", "hi": "मोहित नहीं होता"}
    ],
    "translation": {
      "en": "Just as the soul within this body passes through childhood, youth, and old age, so too it passes into another body at death. A person of steady wisdom is not disturbed by this change.",
      "hi": "जिस प्रकार देहधारी आत्मा इस शरीर में बाल्यावस्था, युवावस्था और वृद्धावस्था से होकर गुजरती है, उसी प्रकार मृत्यु के समय वह दूसरे शरीर को प्राप्त होती है। धीर पुरुष इस परिवर्तन से विचलित नहीं होता।"
    },
    "audioUrl": "audio/2.13_final.m4a"
  },
  {
    "id": "bg-2-20", "name": "BG 2.20", "book": "bg", "sub": "na jāyate mriyate vā kadācin", "badge": "गी",
    "lines": ["na jāyate mriyate vā kadācin", "nāyaṁ bhūtvā bhavitā vā na bhūyaḥ", "ajo nityaḥ śāśvato 'yaṁ purāṇo", "na hanyate hanyamāne śarīre"],
    "words": [
      {"sa": "na jāyate", "en": "is never born", "hi": "जन्म नहीं लेती"},
      {"sa": "mriyate", "en": "dies", "hi": "मरती है"},
      {"sa": "vā", "en": "or", "hi": "अथवा"},
      {"sa": "kadācit", "en": "at any time", "hi": "कभी भी"},
      {"sa": "na ayam", "en": "this (soul) never", "hi": "यह आत्मा कभी नहीं"},
      {"sa": "bhūtvā", "en": "having come into being", "hi": "उत्पन्न होकर"},
      {"sa": "bhavitā", "en": "will come to be", "hi": "होगी"},
      {"sa": "vā na bhūyaḥ", "en": "or cease to be again", "hi": "अथवा फिर नहीं होगी"},
      {"sa": "ajaḥ", "en": "unborn", "hi": "अजन्मा"},
      {"sa": "nityaḥ", "en": "eternal", "hi": "नित्य"},
      {"sa": "śāśvataḥ", "en": "permanent", "hi": "शाश्वत"},
      {"sa": "ayam", "en": "this", "hi": "यह"},
      {"sa": "purāṇaḥ", "en": "the oldest/primeval", "hi": "पुरातन/सनातन"},
      {"sa": "na hanyate", "en": "is not slain", "hi": "मारी नहीं जाती"},
      {"sa": "hanyamāne śarīre", "en": "when the body is slain", "hi": "शरीर के मारे जाने पर"}
    ],
    "translation": {
      "en": "The soul is never born and never dies; it does not come into being and then cease to exist. It is unborn, eternal, ever-existing, and primordial. It is not killed when the body is killed.",
      "hi": "आत्मा न कभी जन्म लेती है और न कभी मरती है; न यह किसी समय उत्पन्न हुई है और न होगी। यह अजन्मा, नित्य, शाश्वत और पुरातन है। शरीर के मारे जाने पर भी यह मारी नहीं जाती।"
    },
    "audioUrl": "audio/2.20_final.m4a"
  },
  {
    "id": "bg-2-44", "name": "BG 2.44", "book": "bg", "sub": "bhogaiśvarya-prasaktānāṁ", "badge": "गी",
    "lines": ["bhogaiśvarya-prasaktānāṁ", "tayāpahṛta-cetasām", "vyavasāyātmikā buddhiḥ", "samādhau na vidhīyate"],
    "words": [
      {"sa": "bhoga", "en": "sense enjoyment", "hi": "भोग"},
      {"sa": "aiśvarya", "en": "and material opulence", "hi": "और ऐश्वर्य में"},
